From: OTM receiver <otm@ffnef.de>
Subject: [PATCH] mt76-test: allow state tx_cont

The kernel accepts MT76_TM_STATE_TX_CONT (continuous waveform tx, mt7915
passes the bandwidth incl. CMD_CBW_10MHZ to the RF test command), but the
CLI had no name for it. Needed for the ITS-G5 10 MHz experiment.

diff --git a/tools/fields.c b/tools/fields.c
index e3f6908..4bb2d0c 100644
--- a/tools/fields.c
+++ b/tools/fields.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ static const char * const testmode_state[] = {
 	[MT76_TM_STATE_IDLE] = "idle",
 	[MT76_TM_STATE_TX_FRAMES] = "tx_frames",
 	[MT76_TM_STATE_RX_FRAMES] = "rx_frames",
+	[MT76_TM_STATE_TX_CONT] = "tx_cont",
 };
 
 static const char * const testmode_tx_mode[] = {
